ctician, Weight of the World, Cleansing Drop, Traveler's Rest — each mapped to a state moment (idle / loading / queued / running / all-clear / retry / unknown / done).\n\nGame-specific devices (audio, camera moves, screen-shake, HUD icons, world triggers) are dropped or mapped onto vocabulary we already have: star dots from the parked backdrop, loop-perfect dot particles (ripples/droplets/sketch-lines), the runtime speech bubble, and the existing dot-matrix Lucide doodles. Full translation + build plan in **`ui/brand/ascii/SCENES.md`**. These are **not built in this PR** — they'll be prototyped as samples first (as every prior visual call in this system was), then baked.\n\nScenery behind the beetle (sun/moon/clouds, parallax) was explored and **parked as overkill for v1**. The full design + a build recipe are preserved in `ui/brand/ascii/BACKDROPS.md`.\n\n- Both UIs built clean locally at commit time; not re-verified post-commit (reviewer will validate).\n- The beetle-scene files also carried **pre-existing uncommitted** ASCII brand work (the runtime speech-bubble player, the `.empty-scene` state moment) that shares the same files, so it's bundled here — the diff is broader than just this session's square-cell/legs edits. Unrelated in-flight work (helm/deploy, k8s executor, Justfile, Doodle components, RunPipeline) was deliberately excluded.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}